  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "Let $\\mathrm{S}=\\{1,2, \\ldots . ., 20\\}$. A subset $\\mathrm{B}$ of $\\mathrm{S}$ is said to be \"nice\", if the sum of the elements of $\\mathrm{B}$ is 203 . Than the probability that a randomly chosen subset of $S$ is \"nice\" is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "tACm1",
      "text": "$\\frac{7}{2^{20}}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "zE1HI",
      "text": "$\\frac{5}{2^{20}}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "tkt4O",
      "text": "$\\frac{4}{2^{20}}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "j8UT6",
      "text": "None of the above",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Since total number of subsets of the set $S=2^{20}$\r\n\r\nNow, the sum of all number from 1 to $20=\\frac{20 \\times 21}{2}=210$ Then, find the sets which has sum 7 .\r\n\r\n(1) $\\{7\\}$\r\n\r\n(2) $\\{1,6\\}$\r\n\r\n(3) $\\{2,5\\}$\r\n\r\n(4) $\\{3,4\\}$\r\n\r\n(5) $\\{1,2,4\\}$\r\n\r\nThen, there is only 5 sets which has sum 203\r\n\r\nHence required probability $=\\frac{5}{2^{20}}$",
    "image": null
  },
